		<PackageReleaseNotes>
    [2026-11-02] Route AdminChat large attachments through streaming Workspace processing
    1. Support files above the local parsing limit through a 300 MiB streaming upload endpoint.
    2. Skip full-text extraction for large attachments and expose Workspace/Python batch-processing guidance with file size metadata.
    [2026-11-02] Add shared bilingual contextual documentation help with an iframe dialog, new-window access and page/feature pilots.
    [2026-11-02] Merge live Host metrics and historical resource trends into one linear, zoomable monitor with network throughput and selectable time ranges.
    [2026-11-02] Display average/highest prompt scores and add score/PromptCode sorting to the shared PromptRange picker.
    [2026-11-02] Add the reusable v-prompt-range selector with range/lane filters, keyword search, preview and cursor insertion; integrate both AdminChat composers.
    [2026-11-02] Fix sparse resource-monitor rendering with ECharts 3 and reuse Host panel spacing, borders and header styles.
    [2026-11-02] Restore the GetHostMetrics API binding and show specific global Pivot access denial reasons without changing access policies.
    [2026-11-02] Add streamed large-file Workspace uploads and clean up unsubmitted Chat attachments
    1. Add a multi-file Workspace management upload flow with a 300 MiB per-file limit and tenant-aware ownership checks.
    2. Remove unsubmitted Chat attachment resources through a protected server endpoint and preserve submitted attachment files.
    3. Allow the first Chat turn to be attachment-only and clean up pending resources when changing sessions.
    [2026-11-01] Improve missing custom NeuCharPivot Block handling
    1. Show a friendly placeholder with the missing module UID and Function Code instead of opening an error popup.
    2. Add hover/click guidance and prefilled links to the Pivot and module settings pages.
    3. Preserve missing-block metadata when loading Admin home panels and cover the client fallback behavior with regression tests.
    [2026-10-24] Add private Workspace attachments, bounded local Office/PDF reading and explicit opt-in image vision. Preserve attachment references and original files; never insert binary Base64 into text prompts. Refresh live Markdown styles in the running host.
    1. Upload, paste or drop up to 4 files per message. User uploads do not grant AI write/CLI permission. Read/write size limits come from Workspace configuration and are displayed by the upload control.
    2. DOCX/XLSX/PPTX and text use local extraction; PDF text is read per page, up to 200 pages. Old DOC/XLS/PPT are stored without claiming text extraction. Scanned pages require OCR or explicitly authorized image screenshots; no paid OCR is called automatically.
    3. Document tools paginate up to 4000 characters per call and share a 16000-character per-turn output budget with Workspace listing/reading/search. These are character safeguards, not exact token estimates; model-reported Usage remains authoritative.
    4. Vision is off by default and limited to 2 images per message. Browsers create an EXIF-free JPEG preview with a maximum 1536-pixel side and 512 KB; original files remain unchanged. The selected model must support image input.
    5. Chat messages persist only canonical attachment references and ETags in a nullable AttachmentsJson column. File changes invalidate stale references; generated migrations cover all six database providers.
    6. Admin design-time factories locate the real Senparc.Web configuration when launched from DatabasePlant and refuse to silently target its example database.
    [2026-10-24] Add authenticated HTML browser previews, bounded file/ZIP downloads, and expiring revocable read-only snapshot shares. Anonymous snapshots disable scripts and external resources; keep App_Data and Data Protection keys private and persistent.
    1. Browser preview and downloads require session and Workspace ownership; anonymous links grant read-only access to a frozen HTML snapshot, never directory access or downloads.
    2. Snapshots expire after 1 hour, 24 hours or 7 days; up to 10 active shares per owner. Revocation/expiry blocks new requests, not previously saved copies. Expired snapshots are purged on access or owner management.
    3. HTML and each resource are limited to 2 MB, generated snapshots to 8 MB and 100 resources. ZIPs are limited to 1000 entries, 32 levels and 64 MB uncompressed; per-file reads also honor Workspace configuration.
    4. App_Data/WorkspaceAssetShares is private encrypted storage outside wwwroot. Persist it and Data Protection keys together; replicas must share both. Use HTTPS, exclude capability URLs from access logs and keep App_Data out of static-file mappings/backups accessible to clients.
    5. Fix doubled live Markdown line breaks without changing stream text, paragraphs or code-block whitespace.
    [2026-10-24] Expand Workspace previews while preserving Chat minimum width; render Markdown with a source toggle.
    [2026-10-24] Fix Chat Workspace asset panel template nesting, file entry fields, and split-pane resizing.
